    "is_free": false,
    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Step aboard the MS Estonia which tragically sank on the 28th of September 1994 in the Baltic Sea.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Experience</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on the final voyage of the ill-fated MS Estonia and experience the final moments of the ships tragic demise. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As a passenger, you get to explore the ship in an immersive simulation that accurately depicts the ships final moments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Facing an intense storm and critical system failure, the MS Estonia's life-boat system becomes inoperable, and you must find another way to safety before time runs out or stay aboard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The MS Estonia has never been recreated to this level of detail. The entire exterior of the ship is explorable, with the bridge also being accessible.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Background of the MS Estonia</strong> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The MS Estonia, a tragic chapter in maritime history, was a passenger ferry that sank in the Baltic Sea on September 28, 1994. Departing from Tallinn, Estonia, en route to Stockholm, Sweden, the vessel met its end in a violent storm. The disaster claimed the lives of over 800 passengers and crew, making it one of the worst maritime tragedies of the 20th century.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Note: This is a simulation experience not a story-based game</strong></p>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Step aboard the MS Estonia which tragically sank on the 28th of September 1994 in the Baltic Sea.</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>The Experience</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Embark on the final voyage of the ill-fated MS Estonia and experience the final moments of the ships tragic demise. </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >As a passenger, you get to explore the ship in an immersive simulation that accurately depicts the ships final moments.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Facing an intense storm and critical system failure, the MS Estonia's life-boat system becomes inoperable, and you must find another way to safety before time runs out or stay aboard.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The MS Estonia has never been recreated to this level of detail. The entire exterior of the ship is explorable, with the bridge also being accessible.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" > </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Background of the MS Estonia</strong> </p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The MS Estonia, a tragic chapter in maritime history, was a passenger ferry that sank in the Baltic Sea on September 28, 1994. Departing from Tallinn, Estonia, en route to Stockholm, Sweden, the vessel met its end in a violent storm. The disaster claimed the lives of over 800 passengers and crew, making it one of the worst maritime tragedies of the 20th century.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Note: This is a simulation experience not a story-based game</strong></p>",
    "short_description": "Step into the shoes of a passenger aboard the ill-fated MS Estonia in this immersive simulation. Discover what caused the ship's demise on the tragic day of 28th September 1994. With time running out, are you able to find a way off the ship?",
